-----------------------------
Source: Tanzil Project Uthmani Quran text (Version 1.1)
        https://tanzil.net
Copyright (C) 2007-2025 Tanzil Project
License: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (CC-BY 3.0)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

This copy of the Quran text is carefully produced, highly verified and
continuously monitored by a group of specialists at the Tanzil Project.

Terms of use (per the original Tanzil Project copyright notice):

  - Permission is granted to copy and distribute verbatim copies of this
    text, but changing it is not allowed.
  - This Quran text can be used in any website or application, provided
    that its source (Tanzil Project) is clearly indicated, and a link is
    made to https://tanzil.net to enable users to keep track of changes.
  - This copyright notice shall be included in all verbatim copies of the
    text, and shall be reproduced appropriately in all files derived from
    or containing a substantial portion of this text.

Please check updates at: https://tanzil.net/updates/

The data in resources/quran-uthmani.json was mechanically converted from
Tanzil's official Uthmani XML export (same Version 1.1 text, same
copyright block reproduced above) into a flat JSON array of
{ surahNumber, surahName, ayahNumber, text } objects. The Arabic text and
surah names were not altered, normalised, or "cleaned" in any way; only
the container format was changed from XML to JSON.

No translation of the Quran is bundled with this application.

resources/fonts/AmiriQuran.ttf
-------------------------------
Source: Amiri Quran, from the Amiri type project
        https://github.com/aliftype/amiri/releases/download/1.003/Amiri-1.003.zip
        (release 1.003, file AmiriQuran.ttf from the release archive)
Copyright 2010-2022 The Amiri Project Authors (https://github.com/aliftype/amiri)
License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-1.1)
         https://openfontlicense.org/

The font's own embedded metadata (its TrueType `name` table) identifies it as
Family "Amiri Quran", Full name "Amiri Quran Regular", Manufacturer
"Alif Type", and carries the OFL 1.1 license string directly in its
nameID 13 record — this was verified programmatically before bundling by
reading the font's binary name table, not by trusting the filename.

The full OFL 1.1 license text (as shipped in the upstream release archive's
OFL.txt) applies to this font. It permits bundling, embedding, and
redistribution with this application; the font itself may not be sold on
its own and its Reserved Font Name ("Amiri Quran") may not be used to
label a modified version.

OFL 1.1 condition 2 requires that the license text be included with, not
merely linked from, each copy — so the full text is bundled verbatim at
resources/fonts/OFL.txt (copied unmodified from the same release archive,
Amiri-1.003.zip, file OFL.txt).

resources/icons/tray.png
--------------------------
This is not a third-party asset. It is a 32x32 placeholder tray icon
generated programmatically during this project's first implementation task.
It is original work created for and owned by this project, not sourced from
any external artwork. It is a placeholder pending final artwork.

resources/sounds/notify.wav
----------------------------
This is not a third-party asset. It is a short, soft two-tone chime
(660 Hz then 880 Hz, ~0.6s, exponential fade-out) synthesised
programmatically for this project — mono, 16-bit PCM, 22.05 kHz.

Generated by, and reproducible from, tools/make-chime.mjs (run
`node tools/make-chime.mjs` to regenerate the identical file). Being
self-generated, it carries no third-party licensing terms; it is original
work created for and owned by this project.
